    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Publicly, Heinrich Himmler was Adolf Hitler's right hand, leader of the Gestapo and the Order of the Death's Head, and Prince Gustav Breidenstein's mortal ghoul before Maxwell Ldescu Embraced him into the Tremere in 1945. Secretly, he is unbondable &mdash; the Blood Bond his sire relied upon never took &mdash; and has since defected to the Sabbat, becoming antitribu without the tell-tale brow-mark the Vaulderie normally leaves, so that no Tremere suspects his true allegiance. Using the alias Frederick Werther, he manipulates Dieter Kotlar and the Final Reich as tools to expand Sabbat influence throughout Berlin and eventually all of Europe, all while playing the loyal, deferential childe to his unknowing sire Ldescu. He follows the Path of Death and the Soul.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Normally quiet; when engaged, keep your comments short and succinct. Defer in all things to Ldescu, feigning penance for having disappeared after your Embrace. Rarely smile, and when you do, make it a challenge.</p>",
    "notes": "Introduces himself to strangers as Frederick Werther. Secretly leads Berlin's Sabbat and controls the Final Reich through Dieter Kotlar. Completely unbondable; the Vaulderie leaves no mark on him, so his own clan does not suspect his Sabbat allegiance. Convert Disciplines by adding owned power Items (Auspex, Dominate, Presence, Thaumaturgy, Vicissitude) at Storyteller discretion.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
